"Questors banned spreading Insight to non-Questors; Davrar warns those about to break the ban."
"A Questor who names a barred secret winces at an unseen warning from Davrar."
"The first arcane blight forced a Conclave limiting which Insights may be taught to mortals."
"Those limits on teaching Insights to mortals still hold."
"By an old council resolution, Davrar marks whenever a teleportation Insight is shared."
"That resolution was made to stop teleportation kill squads."
"The secret of the Seals is a Conclave-restricted Insight."
"Nuclear fission is among the most restricted Insights of all, a secret since the Ending of Magic."
"Some Insights belong to known Questor builds and would be traced if taught to a mortal."
"Grand Insights are major Insights Questors can grant."
"Questors buy Insights cheaply with points, or trade favors for them."
"Many modern Questors own powerful Insights they did not develop and do not understand."
"The ancient Kalis empire spread Insights freely, putting wizardry into mortal hands."
"The first arcane blight was born of a mortal hacking the Seals with unrestrained Insight."
"Later, Badud wanted Teleport and Mass Teleport made common Insights in Giantsrest."
"Nathan Lark is outside the Insight restrictions that bind others."
"Later, Nathan taught Stella fusion, fission, E=mc2 and binding energy as one nuclear Insight."
"Nathan made the Heirs swear never to share or write down that nuclear Insight."
"Years later the Heirs' book of Earth-science Insights was called the Liber Physicae."
"Years later Gemore held a library of Insights founded by the Heirs."
"Ushia buries Insights in ancient tomes for readers to find."
"Nathan's antimagic Insight is his own invention, uniquely weighty, unknown to others."
"Years later Nathan pre-built Insights in his mind palace to deploy mid-fight."
